    "problem_statement": "QRCode generation fails with UnboundLocalError for large versions\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating QR codes with large versions (like version 27), the code fails with an UnboundLocalError indicating that a local variable 'bits' is referenced before assignment.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\n# This fails with UnboundLocalError\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(version=27)\nqr.add_data('a')\nqr.make(fit=False)\n```\n\nThe error also occurs when using the optimize feature with certain text patterns:\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\ntext = 'A1abc12345123451234512345def1HELLOHELLOHELLOHELLOa' * 5\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data(text)\nqr.make()  # This also triggers the same error\n```\n\nBoth cases result in:\n```\nUnboundLocalError: local variable 'bits' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThe issue seems to affect QR code generation when the version requires type number setup, which happens for versions 7 and above."
